The optimized multiplier initially stores multiplicand in a temporary register and product  = 0;
If current multiplier bit is 1 then
  add the temp register to the product.
[If multiplier bit is 0 there is no need to add it to the product.]

Left shift the temp register no matter what the outcome of the previous condition is.
[This is to mimic how in actual multiplication too, the multiplicand is shifted once and then added together]

Repeat the above steps for all the bits of multiplier (right to left).
